## 7. Apply Aggregate Functions

### 7.1 COUNT() – Count Total Sales Transactions

```sql
SELECT COUNT(*) AS TotalTransactions
FROM Sales;
```

**Purpose:** Counts the total number of sales transactions.

### 7.2 SUM() – Calculate Total Quantity Sold

```sql
SELECT SUM(Quantity) AS TotalQuantitySold
FROM Sales;
```

**Purpose:** Calculates the total number of product units sold.

### 7.3 AVG() – Calculate Average Product Price

```sql
SELECT AVG(Price) AS AverageProductPrice
FROM Product;
```

**Purpose:** Calculates the average price of all products.

### 7.4 MIN() – Find the Lowest Product Price

```sql
SELECT MIN(Price) AS LowestProductPrice
FROM Product;
```

**Purpose:** Identifies the least expensive product price.

### 7.5 MAX() – Find the Highest Product Price

```sql
SELECT MAX(Price) AS HighestProductPrice
FROM Product;
```

**Purpose:** Identifies the most expensive product price.

## 8. Generate Total Sales Reports

### 8.1 Calculate Total Sales Revenue

```sql
SELECT SUM(P.Price * S.Quantity) AS TotalSalesRevenue
FROM Sales S
JOIN Product P
ON S.ProductID = P.ProductID;
```

**Purpose:** Calculates total sales revenue using product prices and quantities sold.

### 8.2 Display Sales Transaction Details

```sql
SELECT
    S.SaleID,
    C.CustomerName,
    P.ProductName,
    P.Category,
    S.Quantity,
    P.Price,
    P.Price * S.Quantity AS TotalAmount,
    S.SaleDate
FROM Sales S
JOIN Customer C
ON S.CustomerID = C.CustomerID
JOIN Product P
ON S.ProductID = P.ProductID
ORDER BY S.SaleDate;
```

**Purpose:** Displays complete sales transaction details, including customer, product, quantity, and total amount.

### 8.3 Generate Date-Wise Sales Report

```sql
SELECT
    SaleDate,
    SUM(P.Price * S.Quantity) AS DailySales
FROM Sales S
JOIN Product P
ON S.ProductID = P.ProductID
GROUP BY SaleDate
ORDER BY SaleDate;
```

**Purpose:** Calculates daily sales revenue.

## 9. Find Top Customers Based on Purchase Amount

```sql
SELECT
    C.CustomerID,
    C.CustomerName,
    SUM(P.Price * S.Quantity) AS TotalPurchaseAmount
FROM Customer C
JOIN Sales S
ON C.CustomerID = S.CustomerID
JOIN Product P
ON S.ProductID = P.ProductID
GROUP BY C.CustomerID, C.CustomerName
ORDER BY TotalPurchaseAmount DESC
LIMIT 5;
```

**Purpose:** Ranks customers according to their total purchase amounts and displays the top five customers.

## 10. Identify Best-Selling Products

### 10.1 Rank Products by Quantity Sold

```sql
SELECT
    P.ProductID,
    P.ProductName,
    SUM(S.Quantity) AS TotalQuantitySold
FROM Product P
JOIN Sales S
ON P.ProductID = S.ProductID
GROUP BY P.ProductID, P.ProductName
ORDER BY TotalQuantitySold DESC;
```

**Purpose:** Identifies the best-selling products based on the total number of units sold.

### 10.2 Rank Products by Sales Revenue

```sql
SELECT
    P.ProductID,
    P.ProductName,
    SUM(P.Price * S.Quantity) AS TotalRevenue
FROM Product P
JOIN Sales S
ON P.ProductID = S.ProductID
GROUP BY P.ProductID, P.ProductName
ORDER BY TotalRevenue DESC;
```

**Purpose:** Identifies products that generate the highest sales revenue.

## 11. Perform Category-Wise Sales Analysis

### 11.1 Calculate Total Sales by Category

```sql
SELECT
    P.Category,
    SUM(P.Price * S.Quantity) AS CategorySales
FROM Product P
JOIN Sales S
ON P.ProductID = S.ProductID
GROUP BY P.Category
ORDER BY CategorySales DESC;
```

**Purpose:** Compares sales revenue across product categories.

### 11.2 Calculate Category-Wise Quantity Sold

```sql
SELECT
    P.Category,
    SUM(S.Quantity) AS TotalQuantitySold
FROM Product P
JOIN Sales S
ON P.ProductID = S.ProductID
GROUP BY P.Category
ORDER BY TotalQuantitySold DESC;
```

**Purpose:** Determines which product categories sell the highest number of units.

### 11.3 Calculate Average Sales Amount by Category

```sql
SELECT
    P.Category,
    AVG(P.Price * S.Quantity) AS AverageSalesAmount
FROM Product P
JOIN Sales S
ON P.ProductID = S.ProductID
GROUP BY P.Category
ORDER BY AverageSalesAmount DESC;
```

**Purpose:** Calculates the average transaction value for each product category.

## 12. Generate a Complete Sales Summary

```sql
SELECT
    COUNT(*) AS TotalTransactions,
    SUM(S.Quantity) AS TotalUnitsSold,
    SUM(P.Price * S.Quantity) AS TotalRevenue,
    AVG(P.Price * S.Quantity) AS AverageTransactionAmount,
    MIN(P.Price * S.Quantity) AS MinimumLineItemAmount,
    MAX(P.Price * S.Quantity) AS MaximumLineItemAmount
FROM Sales S
JOIN Product P
ON S.ProductID = P.ProductID;
```

**Purpose:** Generates an overall summary of sales performance using all five aggregate functions.

**Note:** The minimum and maximum values in this query represent individual sales line amounts, not complete transaction totals when a transaction can contain multiple products.

